.TH CRYPTOTRACKIN 1 "2026" "cryptotrackin 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cryptotrackin \- trace cryptocurrency wallet transactions and flag risk indicators
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cryptotrackin
[\fB\-a\fR \fIADDRESS\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILIMIT\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-history\fR]
[\fB\-\-web\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fIHOST\fR] [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-banner\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cryptotrackin
is a blockchain transaction forensics tool. Given a Bitcoin, Ethereum, or
Litecoin
wallet address, it retrieves transaction history, builds a transaction
flow graph, and flags risk indicators such as interaction with known
flagged addresses or fan-out patterns typical of fund obfuscation.

Intended for legitimate security research, blockchain forensics
training, and authorized investigation contexts (e.g. tracing
ransomware payment addresses on practice/test data or with proper
authorization).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Wallet address to trace (BTC, ETH, or LTC).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit " " \fILIMIT\fR
Maximum number of transactions to fetch (default: 20).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output raw JSON instead of formatted text.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Show recent search history from the local cache.
.TP
.B \-\-web
Launch the web dashboard (graphical flow view) instead of CLI mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fIHOST\fR
Host to bind the web dashboard to (default: 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Port for the web dashboard (default: 5000).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Suppress the ASCII banner on startup.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Trace a Bitcoin address:
.B cryptotrackin \-a 1A1zP1eP5QGefi2DMPTfTL5SLmv7DivfNa
.TP
Launch the interactive web dashboard:
.B cryptotrackin \-\-web
.TP
View recent search history:
.B cryptotrackin \-\-history
.SH FILES
.I ~/.cryptotrackin/tracker.db
.RS
Local SQLite cache of search history.
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
Built by ambatron_ctrlz as a cybersecurity coursework / internship project.
